WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.100
Untangle turns a long email,

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:07.200
letter or assignment brief into a checklist you can work through one step at a time.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.240
This is a made-up financial aid email, the kind of message that is easy to misread.

00:00:13.242 --> 00:00:16.664
Press Untangle it, and the email becomes four steps,

00:00:16.664 --> 00:00:19.953
three documents to have ready, and three warnings.

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:24.362
It all happens in your browser; nothing you paste is sent anywhere.

00:00:25.365 --> 00:00:29.505
Each step is a short instruction with its due date and any condition,

00:00:29.505 --> 00:00:32.505
and the exact original sentence is one click away.

00:00:32.505 --> 00:00:35.985
A window that counts from something you have not done yet,

00:00:35.985 --> 00:00:39.525
like this one, keeps its wording instead of a guessed date.

00:00:40.528 --> 00:00:43.846
Focus mode shows one step per screen in large type,

00:00:43.846 --> 00:00:45.993
starting with what to have ready.

00:00:45.993 --> 00:00:51.328
Done, Skip for now and Back work with the mouse, or with Enter and the arrow keys.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:57.075
Larger text, wider spacing and an easy-read font apply to the whole page,

00:00:57.075 --> 00:00:59.610
and your progress stays on this device.

00:01:00.612 --> 00:01:03.942
Finally, the dated steps go to your calendar with reminders,

00:01:03.942 --> 00:01:06.772
or the whole checklist can be copied as plain text.
